## Names that never bind to a native library (ImplementationPlan.md 5.14.2
## N1-N4 and N-2, M24.d (1); helpers-switches 2.5). msil-ld resolves an
## undefined symbol from objects, archive members, the '<trailer>' input and
## native libraries, in that order, and skips every native library for these
## names, whichever one on the command line exports them:
## - N1, the '__' names of lto::LTO::getRuntimeLibcallSymbols for the codegen
##   triple (compiler-rt's builtins): __extendhfsf2, which the legalizer
##   calls for an fpext of half, is never taken from a libgcc_s.so.1
##   stand-in (or a DLL on windows-msvc). Its undefined-symbol report gains,
##   after the first line and before the '>>> referenced by' lines,
##     >>> a compiler runtime helper: link the toolchain's helper archive clang_rt.builtins
##   An archive member that defines it wins over the native library in either
##   order (helpers-switches E4); a weak reference stays unbound (the trap
##   stub '<msil>undef_<name>', no P/Invoke). The C library's own entry
##   points that the set also lists (isCLibraryName) are not N1 and still
##   bind natively, with no line: on linux-gnu __memcpy_chk, __memmove_chk
##   and __memset_chk (which glibc's _FORTIFY_SOURCE wrappers call) and
##   __stack_chk_fail to libc.so.6, the stack protector's guard
##   __stack_chk_guard as a data import (through libc.so.6's dlopen and
##   dlsym), and libm's __<function>_finite entry points (matched by their
##   suffix; here __exp_finite and __powf_finite) to libm.so.6; on
##   windows-msvc the C runtime's __chkstk, __security_check_cookie and the
##   data __security_cookie (to a VCRUNTIME140.dll import library).
## - N2, '__atomic_*' (libatomic's interface): on Linux triples it binds to a
##   libatomic.so.1 stand-in, as a native build links it (user decisions
##   R4/R5 (5), N-3), and without one the report gains
##     >>> an atomic operation: link with -latomic, as a native build does
##   On Windows triples it never binds natively (here to a libatomic-1.dll
##   import library):
##     >>> an atomic operation (libatomic's interface)
##   The objects call __atomic_load_4 directly, so M30's inline atomics leave
##   this test alone.
## - N3, '__msil_*' (cli::isToolchainName): never from a native library (an
##   ELF shared object, a DLL import library) or from another assembly (a
##   toolchain library that msil-ld -shared built and that exports it):
##     >>> a toolchain helper: link the toolchain's helper archive clang_rt.builtins; if it is linked, the object needs a newer toolchain
##   An archive member supplies it.
## - N4, the setjmp family: not a report but an error per referencing file
##   and name,
##     <file>: '<name>' cannot be bound to a native library: setjmp and longjmp are lowered by the compiler
##   whether or not a native library exports the name. The objects call all
##   ten: _setjmp, setjmp, __sigsetjmp, sigsetjmp, longjmp, _longjmp,
##   siglongjmp and __longjmp_chk on Linux, and _setjmpex, _setjmp, _setjmp3
##   and longjmp on windows-msvc. An object definition resolves them. From
##   M27 the backend lowers every such call, so only older objects meet this
##   error.
## - Import names: the native libraries are searched by a symbol's import
##   name (msil-import-name, C's import_name) when it has one, so the guards
##   also test that name. Ordinary symbols imported as __extendhfsf2 (N1),
##   _setjmp (N4) and __msil_foo (N3) never bind to the libraries that export
##   those names. 5.14.2 gives import names no text, so each stays today's
##   'undefined symbol: <symbol>', keyed on the symbol name, without a class
##   line or N4's error, and a weak reference keeps its trap stub. Objects
##   and LTO images are checked through their objects' import attributes,
##   --lto-emit-asm text through the merged module's (the import annotation).
## Through CIL objects (llc -filetype=obj), LTO with an image (the reference
## that code generation creates after LTO names '<output>.lto.o') and
## --lto-emit-asm. In whole-program text the fpext of half stays the
## backend's helper error, D14's text, which M25 rewords.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: yaml2obj libgcc.yaml -o libgcc.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libgcc_s.so.1 libgcc.o -o libgcc_s.so.1
# RUN: yaml2obj libc.yaml -o libc.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libc.so.6 libc.o -o libc.so.6
# RUN: yaml2obj libm.yaml -o libm.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libm.so.6 libm.o -o libm.so.6
# RUN: yaml2obj atomic.yaml -o atomic.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libatomic.so.1 atomic.o -o libatomic.so.1
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:x64 /def:helpers.def /out:helpers.lib
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:x64 /def:atomic.def /out:atomic.lib
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:x64 /def:vcruntime.def /out:vcruntime.lib
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj half.ll -o half.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj ref2.ll -o ref2.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj ext.ll -o ext.o
# RUN: llvm-ar rcs libhelp.a ext.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj weak.ll -o weak.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj chk.ll -o chk.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj clib.ll -o clib.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj crt-win.ll -o crt-win.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj atom.ll -o atom.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj atom-win.ll -o atom-win.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj help-win.ll -o help-win.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj foo.ll -o foo.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj tl.ll -o tl.o
# RUN: llvm-ar rcs libtl.a tl.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj use.ll -o use.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj sj.ll -o sj.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj sj2.ll -o sj2.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj sjdef.ll -o sjdef.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj sj-win.ll -o sj-win.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj imp.ll -o imp.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj impweak.ll -o impweak.o
# RUN: llvm-as half.ll -o half.bc
# RUN: llvm-as direct.ll -o direct.bc
# RUN: llvm-as weak.ll -o weak.bc
# RUN: llvm-as chk.ll -o chk.bc
# RUN: llvm-as clib.ll -o clib.bc
# RUN: llvm-as crt-win.ll -o crt-win.bc
# RUN: llvm-as atom.ll -o atom.bc
# RUN: llvm-as atom-win.ll -o atom-win.bc
# RUN: llvm-as foo.ll -o foo.bc
# RUN: llvm-as sj.ll -o sj.bc
# RUN: llvm-as imp.ll -o imp.bc
# RUN: llvm-as impweak.ll -o impweak.bc

# DEFINE: %{crash} = --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"
# DEFINE: %{err} = FileCheck %s %{crash} --implicit-check-not=error: --implicit-check-not=warning: \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not=">>>"

## The N1 name __extendhfsf2 stays undefined although libgcc_s.so.1 exports
## it; the report is the same without the library.
# RUN: not msil-ld half.o libgcc_s.so.1 -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N1 -DREF=half.o
# RUN: not msil-ld half.o -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N1 -DREF=half.o
# N1:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: __extendhfsf2{{$}}
# N1-NEXT: {{^}}>>> a compiler runtime helper: link the toolchain's helper archive clang_rt.builtins{{$}}
# N1-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by [[REF]]:(main){{$}}

## Two referencing files: the line once, then a '>>> referenced by' line for
## each (--no-gc-sections keeps ref2.o's function).
# RUN: not msil-ld --no-gc-sections half.o ref2.o libgcc_s.so.1 -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N1-TWO
# N1-TWO:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: __extendhfsf2{{$}}
# N1-TWO-NEXT: {{^}}>>> a compiler runtime helper: link the toolchain's helper archive clang_rt.builtins{{$}}
# N1-TWO-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by half.o:(main){{$}}
# N1-TWO-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by ref2.o:(ext2){{$}}

## LTO: a direct call is a bitcode reference; the legalizer's call exists
## only after LTO, in the LTO object.
# RUN: not msil-ld direct.bc libgcc_s.so.1 -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N1 -DREF=direct.bc
# RUN: not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm direct.bc libgcc_s.so.1 -o x.il 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N1 -DREF=direct.bc
# RUN: not msil-ld half.bc libgcc_s.so.1 -o half-lto.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N1 -DREF=half-lto.exe.lto.o
# RUN: not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm half.bc libgcc_s.so.1 -o x.il 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | %{err} --check-prefix=N1-TEXT --implicit-check-not=pinvokeimpl --implicit-check-not=libgcc_s
# N1-TEXT: {{^}}msil-ld: error: runtime helper '__extendhfsf2' is not available for MSIL yet (phase 3){{$}}

## An archive member wins over the native library in either order.
# RUN: msil-ld half.o libhelp.a libgcc_s.so.1 -o ar1.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: msil-ld half.o libgcc_s.so.1 libhelp.a -o ar2.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump ar1.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ARCHIVE --implicit-check-not=pinvokeimpl \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not=moduleref
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump ar2.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ARCHIVE --implicit-check-not=pinvokeimpl \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not=moduleref
# ARCHIVE: {{^}}  .method '__extendhfsf2' float32(int32) flags=0x0016 impl=0x0000{{$}}
# ARCHIVE: {{^}}    L{{[0-9]+}}: call float32(int32) '<Module>'::'__extendhfsf2'{{$}}

## A weak reference is not bound natively either: the trap stub.
# RUN: msil-ld weak.o libgcc_s.so.1 -o weak.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump weak.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WEAK --implicit-check-not=pinvokeimpl \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not=moduleref
# RUN: msil-ld weak.bc libgcc_s.so.1 -o weak-lto.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump weak-lto.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WEAK --implicit-check-not=pinvokeimpl \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not=moduleref
# WEAK:      {{^}}  .method '<msil>undef___extendhfsf2' float32(int32) flags=0x0013 impl=0x0000{{$}}
# WEAK:      {{^}}    L{{[0-9]+}}: throw{{$}}
# WEAK:      {{^}}  .method 'main' int32() flags=0x0016 impl=0x0000{{$}}
# WEAK:      {{^}}    L{{[0-9]+}}: call float32(int32) '<Module>'::'<msil>undef___extendhfsf2'{{$}}

## The C library's checked entry points bind natively: objects, LTO with an
## image and --lto-emit-asm (non-constant sizes, so nothing folds them into
## memcpy, memmove or memset).
# RUN: msil-ld chk.o libc.so.6 -o chk.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump chk.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHK
# RUN: msil-ld chk.bc libc.so.6 -o chk-lto.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump chk-lto.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHK
# CHK:      {{^}}moduleref 'libc.so.6'{{$}}
# CHK:      {{^}}  .method '__memcpy_chk' native int(native int, native int, native int, native int) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CHK-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libc.so.6' entry '__memcpy_chk' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CHK-NEXT: {{^}}  .method '__memmove_chk' native int(native int, native int, native int, native int) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CHK-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libc.so.6' entry '__memmove_chk' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CHK-NEXT: {{^}}  .method '__memset_chk' native int(native int, int32, native int, native int) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CHK-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libc.so.6' entry '__memset_chk' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CHK-NEXT: {{^}}  .method '__stack_chk_fail' void() flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CHK-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libc.so.6' entry '__stack_chk_fail' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# RUN: msil-ld --lto-emit-asm chk.bc libc.so.6 -o chk.il 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHK-TEXT --input-file=chk.il
# CHK-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libc.so.6" nomangle cdecl) native int '__memcpy_chk'(native int, native int, native int, native int) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CHK-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libc.so.6" nomangle cdecl) native int '__memmove_chk'(native int, native int, native int, native int) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CHK-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libc.so.6" nomangle cdecl) native int '__memset_chk'(native int, int32, native int, native int) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CHK-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libc.so.6" nomangle cdecl) void '__stack_chk_fail'() cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}

## The C library's other names in the set bind natively too, with no N1
## line (the links print nothing): on linux-gnu the guard __stack_chk_guard
## is a data import that '<msil>init_dataimports' fills through libc.so.6's
## dlopen and dlsym, and libm's _finite entry points are P/Invokes; objects,
## LTO with an image and --lto-emit-asm.
# RUN: msil-ld clib.o libc.so.6 libm.so.6 -o clib.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump clib.exe > clib.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLIB --input-file=clib.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/dataimports.py clib.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLIB-DATA
# RUN: msil-ld clib.bc libc.so.6 libm.so.6 -o clib-lto.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump clib-lto.exe > clib-lto.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLIB --input-file=clib-lto.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/dataimports.py clib-lto.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLIB-DATA
# CLIB:      {{^}}  .method '__exp_finite' float64(float64) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CLIB-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libm.so.6' entry '__exp_finite' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CLIB-NEXT: {{^}}  .method '__powf_finite' float32(float32, float32) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CLIB-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libm.so.6' entry '__powf_finite' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CLIB-NEXT: {{^}}  .method 'dlopen' native int(native int, int32) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CLIB-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libc.so.6' entry 'dlopen' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CLIB-NEXT: {{^}}  .method 'dlsym' native int(native int, native int) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CLIB-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libc.so.6' entry 'dlsym' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CLIB-DATA:     {{^}}import __stack_chk_guard = libc.so.6!__stack_chk_guard{{$}}
# CLIB-DATA-NOT: {{.}}
# RUN: msil-ld --lto-emit-asm clib.bc libc.so.6 libm.so.6 -o clib.il 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLIB-TEXT --input-file=clib.il
# CLIB-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libm.so.6" nomangle cdecl) float64 '__exp_finite'(float64) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CLIB-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libm.so.6" nomangle cdecl) float32 '__powf_finite'(float32, float32) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CLIB-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libc.so.6" nomangle cdecl) native int 'dlopen'(native int, int32) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CLIB-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libc.so.6" nomangle cdecl) native int 'dlsym'(native int, native int) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CLIB-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.field public static native int '__stack_chk_guard'{{$}}
# CLIB-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}  ldstr "libc.so.6"{{$}}
# CLIB-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}  ldstr "__stack_chk_guard"{{$}}
# CLIB-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}  stsfld native int '__stack_chk_guard'{{$}}

## On windows-msvc the C runtime's __chkstk and __security_check_cookie are
## P/Invokes into the VCRUNTIME140.dll stand-in and its __security_cookie a
## data import (through kernel32.dll's LoadLibraryW and GetProcAddress);
## objects, LTO with an image and --lto-emit-asm.
# RUN: msil-ld crt-win.o vcruntime.lib -o crt-win.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump crt-win.exe > crt-win.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CRT --input-file=crt-win.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/dataimports.py crt-win.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CRT-DATA
# RUN: msil-ld crt-win.bc vcruntime.lib -o crt-win-lto.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump crt-win-lto.exe > crt-win-lto.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CRT --input-file=crt-win-lto.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/dataimports.py crt-win-lto.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CRT-DATA
# CRT:      {{^}}  .method '__chkstk' void() flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CRT-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'VCRUNTIME140.dll' entry '__chkstk' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CRT-NEXT: {{^}}  .method '__security_check_cookie' void(native int) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# CRT-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'VCRUNTIME140.dll' entry '__security_check_cookie' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# CRT-DATA:     {{^}}import __security_cookie = VCRUNTIME140.dll!__security_cookie{{$}}
# CRT-DATA-NOT: {{.}}
# RUN: msil-ld --lto-emit-asm crt-win.bc vcruntime.lib -o crt-win.il 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CRT-TEXT --input-file=crt-win.il
# CRT-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("VCRUNTIME140.dll" nomangle cdecl) void '__chkstk'() cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CRT-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("VCRUNTIME140.dll" nomangle cdecl) void '__security_check_cookie'(native int) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# CRT-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}.field public static native int '__security_cookie'{{$}}
# CRT-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}  ldstr "VCRUNTIME140.dll"{{$}}
# CRT-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}  ldstr "__security_cookie"{{$}}
# CRT-TEXT-DAG: {{^}}  stsfld native int '__security_cookie'{{$}}

## Windows: the N1 and N3 names from a DLL's import library stay undefined,
## each with its line.
# RUN: not msil-ld help-win.o helpers.lib -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=WIN-HELP
# WIN-HELP:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: __extendhfsf2{{$}}
# WIN-HELP-NEXT: {{^}}>>> a compiler runtime helper: link the toolchain's helper archive clang_rt.builtins{{$}}
# WIN-HELP-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by help-win.o:(main){{$}}
# WIN-HELP:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: __msil_foo{{$}}
# WIN-HELP-NEXT: {{^}}>>> a toolchain helper: link the toolchain's helper archive clang_rt.builtins; if it is linked, the object needs a newer toolchain{{$}}
# WIN-HELP-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by help-win.o:(main){{$}}

## N2 on Linux: libatomic.so.1 binds __atomic_load_4 (objects, LTO with an
## image, --lto-emit-asm); without it, N2's Linux line.
# RUN: msil-ld atom.o libatomic.so.1 -o atom.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump atom.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ATOMIC
# RUN: msil-ld atom.bc libatomic.so.1 -o atom-lto.exe 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump atom-lto.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ATOMIC
# ATOMIC:      {{^}}moduleref 'libatomic.so.1'{{$}}
# ATOMIC:      {{^}}  .method '__atomic_load_4' int32(native int, int32) flags=0x2093 impl=0x0080{{$}}
# ATOMIC-NEXT: {{^}}    .pinvokeimpl 'libatomic.so.1' entry '__atomic_load_4' flags=0x0201{{$}}
# ATOMIC:      {{^}}    L{{[0-9]+}}: call int32(native int, int32) '<Module>'::'__atomic_load_4'{{$}}
# RUN: msil-ld --lto-emit-asm atom.bc libatomic.so.1 -o atom.il 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ATOMIC-TEXT --input-file=atom.il
# ATOMIC-TEXT: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libatomic.so.1" nomangle cdecl) int32 '__atomic_load_4'(native int, int32) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# RUN: not msil-ld atom.o -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N2-LINUX -DREF=atom.o
# RUN: not msil-ld atom.bc -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N2-LINUX -DREF=atom.bc
# RUN: not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm atom.bc -o x.il 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N2-LINUX -DREF=atom.bc
# N2-LINUX:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: __atomic_load_4{{$}}
# N2-LINUX-NEXT: {{^}}>>> an atomic operation: link with -latomic, as a native build does{{$}}
# N2-LINUX-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by [[REF]]:(main){{$}}

## N2 on Windows: never from a DLL; objects, LTO with an image and
## --lto-emit-asm.
# RUN: not msil-ld atom-win.o atomic.lib -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N2-WIN -DREF=atom-win.o
# RUN: not msil-ld atom-win.o -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N2-WIN -DREF=atom-win.o
# RUN: not msil-ld atom-win.bc atomic.lib -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N2-WIN -DREF=atom-win.bc
# RUN: not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm atom-win.bc atomic.lib -o x.il 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N2-WIN -DREF=atom-win.bc
# N2-WIN:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: __atomic_load_4{{$}}
# N2-WIN-NEXT: {{^}}>>> an atomic operation (libatomic's interface){{$}}
# N2-WIN-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by [[REF]]:(main){{$}}

## The N3 name __msil_foo is never taken from libc.so.6, which exports it,
## and the report is the same without it; objects, LTO with an image and
## --lto-emit-asm.
# RUN: not msil-ld foo.o libc.so.6 -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N3 -DREF=foo.o
# RUN: not msil-ld foo.o -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N3 -DREF=foo.o
# RUN: not msil-ld foo.bc libc.so.6 -o x.exe 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N3 -DREF=foo.bc
# RUN: not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm foo.bc libc.so.6 -o x.il 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=N3 -DREF=foo.bc
# N3:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: __msil_foo{{$}}
# N3-NEXT: {{^}}>>> a toolchain helper: link the toolchain's helper archive clang_rt.builtins; if it is linked, the object needs a newer toolchain{{$}}
# N3-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by [[REF]]:(main){{$}}

## N3 and another assembly: tl.dll (msil-ld -shared) exports __msil_foo and
